                        "form": "die Übergangsriten"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b8ebc48-9ed9-3947-b5ba-72974f6ff25b",
                        "entry_id": "7f907852-a641-3d64-a25a-b65dc89e017d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ethnologisches Konzept, dass im Verlauf des gesellschaftlichen Lebens einer Person zahlreiche Übergänge zwischen Lebensstadien oder sozialen Zuständen vollzogen werden müssen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "73e1b7a6-9f51-4fe7-a417-ffc3f8e8fc91",
                                "sense_id": "5b8ebc48-9ed9-3947-b5ba-72974f6ff25b",
                                "text": "„Jede menschliche Gesellschaft legt Stationen im Leben des Einzelnen fest, denen besondere Bedeutung als Abschluss eines Lebensabschnittes und gleichzeitiger Beginn eines neuen beigemessen wird. Sie werden deshalb öffentlich gefeiert. Wir nennen solche Feste Übergangsriten oder mit dem französischen Ausdruck ‹rites de passage›.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffdd1929-5895-424d-b9b1-fbc04b38a749",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f907852-a641-3d64-a25a-b65dc89e017d",
                        "source_sense_id": "5b8ebc48-9ed9-3947-b5ba-72974f6ff25b",
                        "source_sense_description": "ethnologisches Konzept",
                        "target_lang_word": "通過儀禮",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67aaed33-c218-4a6f-9d02-660f29cc47e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f907852-a641-3d64-a25a-b65dc89e017d",
                        "source_sense_id": "5b8ebc48-9ed9-3947-b5ba-72974f6ff25b",
                        "source_sense_description": "ethnologisches Konzept",
                        "target_lang_word": "rite of passage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rite of passage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6cc9d208-0519-303b-96f5-e6c5e7493bd1",
                                        "entry_id": "518945dc-a1b5-3ee2-b80a-c677919bc525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ceremony or series of ceremonies, often very ritualized, to celebrate a passage or transition from one stage of a person's life to another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bc0e105-5ee3-406a-b3d6-8e37d1de35ca",
                                                "sense_id": "6cc9d208-0519-303b-96f5-e6c5e7493bd1",
                                                "text": "The passage through the jambs would thus signify regeneration or new birth, which was to be followed by either sacrifice or by the purifying rite of passage through the fire; for although the passages are so narrow that they could not be used as ordinary gates, they were wide enough for this purpose, for the sacrificial victims were always youthful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "277cefb9-2689-43b5-9c56-2202d247c2e6",
                                                "sense_id": "6cc9d208-0519-303b-96f5-e6c5e7493bd1",
                                                "text": "The so-called rites of passage, which occupy such a prominent place in the life of a primitive society (ceremonials of birth, naming, puberty, marriage, burial, etc.), are distinguished by formal, and usually very severe, exercises of severance, whereby the mind is radically cut away from the attitudes, attachments, and life patterns of the stage being left behind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "231293bf-efc6-3c66-b33e-1536cae88940",
                                        "entry_id": "518945dc-a1b5-3ee2-b80a-c677919bc525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any significant event or experience that marks a transition from one stage in a person's life to another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b28ba8f4-8f73-4cd4-883f-b0a96533f469",
                                                "sense_id": "231293bf-efc6-3c66-b33e-1536cae88940",
                                                "text": "After John officially attained his majority, Robert bought him his first beer. This is a common American rite of passage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b844a755-272d-485c-b9ab-2a46ab250df1",
                                                "sense_id": "231293bf-efc6-3c66-b33e-1536cae88940",
                                                "text": "In the final, affirming piece, \"They Tell Me...Now I Know,\" the girlchild narrator begins menstruation, thus undergoing her rite of passage into womanhood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba73cc4e-0db3-4b45-ad6d-fe54fe351387",
                                                "sense_id": "231293bf-efc6-3c66-b33e-1536cae88940",
                                                "text": "Not only did these holiday resorts [Butlin's] become a rite of passage for TV's biggest talents – Red Coats comedians, magicians and presenters were often scouted, then sent to perform live at places like the London Palladium, before securing a television contract – but the culture within them meant that the audience were already invested in this type of entertainment once they returned home."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "474a9bbb-3112-43e9-89d4-0ab903db477d",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f907852-a641-3d64-a25a-b65dc89e017d",
                        "source_sense_id": "5b8ebc48-9ed9-3947-b5ba-72974f6ff25b",
                        "source_sense_description": "ethnologisches Konzept",
                        "target_lang_word": "rite de passage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rite de passage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fcb477c2-f3f7-3d10-b4bf-47d6b58d7565",
                                        "entry_id": "59150cd7-ca8b-3a74-adb4-85eda07dc5ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Moment ritualisé, voire marqué par une cérémonie, marquant le passage d’un ou de plusieurs individus d’une étape à une autre de l’existence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67febf85-d563-46f9-83dd-ee98ed0057ee",
                                                "sense_id": "fcb477c2-f3f7-3d10-b4bf-47d6b58d7565",
                                                "text": "Or, leur enchaînement importe autant que leur contenu, et c’est de ce point de vue que van Gennep distingue une certaine classe de rites « qui accompagnent chaque changement de lieu, d’état, de position sociale et d’âge » : ce sont les rites de passage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e41f46c4-ae63-41aa-a3f4-49099bab8d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "fcb477c2-f3f7-3d10-b4bf-47d6b58d7565",
                                                "text": "Au XIXᵉ siècle, le rite de passage à l’âge adulte le plus marquant était sans nul doute le mariage, qui constituait pour les femmes un enjeu bien plus fort que pour les hommes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ce968f1-ca4e-4379-a138-b6ef43b3758e",
                                                "sense_id": "fcb477c2-f3f7-3d10-b4bf-47d6b58d7565",
                                                "text": "On reconnaîtra un rite de passage au fait qu’il marque publiquement la transition d’un statut vers un nouveau statut."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37b6774a-5b42-44ab-a82f-088235a006ab",
                                                "sense_id": "fcb477c2-f3f7-3d10-b4bf-47d6b58d7565",
                                                "text": "Quelles que soient les critiques qu’on leur adresse, ou les nouvelles interprétations qu’on en donne, les « rites de passage », au-delà des changements sociaux, continuent d’inspirer les analyses, depuis la Grèce d’Homère jusqu’à notre XXIᵉ siècle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
